@startuml agentic-vs-autonomous-product
title Agentic vs Autonomous Product Orthogonality ; per ADR-ES-017 §2 + §3 + §8

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

class "Product" as P
class "Agentic Product" as AgP
class "Autonomous Product" as AP
class "Agentic + Autonomous Product" as BothP

P <|-- AgP : specializes (v1.5.0)
P <|-- AP : specializes (v1.6.0)
AgP ..> BothP : combined characterization
AP ..> BothP : combined characterization

note bottom of P
  Per ADR-ES-017 §2 + §3 + §8 + CR-ES-017 §7:
  - Autonomous Product does NOT imply Agentic Product
  - Agentic Product does NOT imply Autonomous Product
  - A Product may be both
  - A Product may be neither
  - The combined state is NOT a new subtype
end note

@enduml
